==Battleground==
*The enemy base here is a [[Surge Base (Enemy Base)|Surge Base]].
*1 [[One Horn]] spawns after 3.33 seconds<sup>100f</sup>.
*Infinite [[Ginger Snache]]s spawn after 6.67 seconds<sup>200f</sup>, delay 23.33~30 seconds<sup>700f~900f</sup>.
*When the base reaches 99% HP:
**1 [[Professor A.]] spawns as the boss.
**1 [[One Horn]] spawns.
**2 [[Rain D.|Rain Ds]] spawn, delay 40~43.33 seconds<sup>1,200f~1,300f</sup>.
**1 [[Croakley]] spawns.

==Strategy==
This stage is mainly about chipping at the Rain Ds. and Professor A as fast as you can so that Croakley doesn't chip your base to death. Although you technically don't need to play with Croakley hitting your base, more units will be able to sneak past and it will be easier.

You can stall the startoff with [[ICat]] by freezing the One Horn. He drops a lot of cash, so you don't need to stall for too long. Once the base is triggered, lure the first Rain D and summon [[Awakened Bahamut Cat]]. With his Explosion [[Talents|Talent]], he will 1v1 the Rain D, although he will probably die to Professor A. Start spawning meatshields to stall out the Professor A and Croakley. Once the One Horn is close enough, send out ICats and use snipers like [[Awakened Mina]], [[Manic Macho Legs]] and [[Masked Grandmaster Cat]] to deal as much damage as you can to the second Rain D and Professor A. Once One Horn dies, use [[Awakened Bahamut Cat]] to finish off the Rain D and do as much damage as you can to Professor A. The [[Thunderbolt]] cannon will help with the timing.

Be wary that if Croakley starts to hit your base, you are essentially on a timer as Croakley is very hard to knockback without very high range units.

==Trivia==
*Prior to [[Version 15.3 Update|Version 15.3]], the stage width was set to 4,500. The change was made because of a bug in how [[:Category:Animated Enemy Bases|Animated Bases]] spawn when not set as bosses.

